ng certificates for SAP under any of its Intermediate CAs (ICA) at the end of 2023. For more information, see DigiCert root and intermediate CA certificate updates 2023.  SAP Cloud Identity Services switches to the G2 ICA and will deploy certificates signed by the new CA for the domains listed below starting in mid-November 2023. This means that the DigiCert Root CA domain certificate will be signed by DigiCert Global Root G2 instead of DigiCert Global Root CA. The following domains are affected:    *.accounts.ondemand.com      *.accounts.cloud.sap      *.accounts.sapcloud.cn      *.trial-accounts.ondemand.com      Action: If your SAP Cloud Identity Services tenants are running on any of the affected domains, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3949 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Root Certificate Replacement\nDescription: DigiCert has deprecated their DigiCert Global Root CA and will stop issuing certificates for SAP under any of its Intermediate CAs (ICA) at the end of 2023. For more information, see DigiCert root and intermediate CA certificate updates 2023.      If your tenant is running on SAP BTP, Neo environment and you are using Identity Provisioning proxy and real-time provisioning scenarios, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2. It replaces the old one DigiCert Global Root CA.   For more information, see Root Certificate Replacement.      If your tenant is running on SAP Cloud Identity Services infrastructure on the domains listed below, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2 starting in mid-November 2023:      *.accounts.ondemand.com      *.accounts.cloud.sap      *.accounts.sapcloud.cn      *.trial-accounts.ondemand.com          For more information, see Root Certificate Replacement in What's New for Identity Authentication.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\n", " running on SAP Cloud Identity Services infrastructure on the domains listed below, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2 starting in mid-November 2023:      *.accounts.ondemand.com      *.accounts.cloud.sap      *.accounts.sapcloud.cn      *.trial-accounts.ondemand.com          For more information, see Root Certificate Replacement in What's New for Identity Authentication.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-06\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3950 ---\nComponent: Java Server\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Java Web Tomcat 8 is deprecated\nDescription: [Periodic reminder] The Java Web Tomcat 8 runtime is deprecated following the official announcement of Apache Tomcat 8.5 end of life. After the end of 2023, we stop providing updates and security patches to it.  Required Action: If you have Java applications running on that runtime, migrate to Java Web Tomcat 9 by the end of 2023. See Migrating from Java Web Tomcat 8 to Java Web Tomcat 9.  For new Java applications, we recommend using Java Web Tomcat 9.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_b8387fe24ea08e6d40fe662d5f5fc96b3dafa5842d9bfa936d629c0c114e168d_v2"}